  "reviewNotes": {
    "tiltCap": "The head rig is one warp on ParamAngleX/Y/Z with pivot (632, 486) and radius ~245 source px, so it reaches past the jaw and any head tilt rotates the whole upper body about that pivot; measured hem-anchored at 280px, an 18 degree tilt moves the chest 17.2px while the legs barely move, which is the split the user reports. Measured trade-off (build/_zoom_review/cap_sweep.py): chest shift 7.1px at cap 18, 5.0px at 12, 3.8px at 9, and motion 9.97 / 8.62 / 7.75. Cap 12 takes the shift down ~30% while keeping more of the accent's motion than cap 9. The lost side-lean is NOT paid to ParamBodyAngleZ: busy-stand has no such track, so the first attempt silently did nothing and the clip lost a third of its motion.",
    "pitchIsNotMotion": "A 6 degree ParamAngleY accent was tried as compensation for the capped tilt and changed the clip's motion energy from 2.109 to 2.106, i.e. nothing. Pitch does not read as motion on this model, so the accent was removed instead of left in the asset. Only roll, the body axes and the hair channels carry the accent."
  }
